				"⠇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				26,
				2
			],
			"Message": "feat(Land): Advance submodules — Output Tauri 2 fix, Sky extensions refresh\n\nAdvance Output and Sky Element submodules with a runtime command-name fix for Tauri 2 and a live Extensions view refresh after extension lifecycle events.\n\nOutput renames the four Shared Process health-check commands from PascalCase (`CocoonExtensionHostHealth`, `CocoonSearchServiceHealth`, `CocoonDebugServiceHealth`, `SharedProcessServiceHealth`) to snake_case to match Mountain's registered handler names. Tauri 2 passes the literal Rust function name as the command identifier without the auto-camel conversion present in Tauri 1, causing `Command not found` errors at runtime. All four per-service health checks now resolve correctly under Tauri 2's strict command-name matching.\n\nSky adds `RefreshExtensionsView`, a guard that invokes `workbench.extensions.action.refreshExtension` after Mountain emits `extensions:install` (VsixInstaller success) or `extensions:uninstall`. VS Code's `IExtensionGalleryService` install pipeline exposes no public hook accessible from outside Cocoon's process boundary, so the command is called programmatically via `Commands.executeCommand`. The refresh is wired after both `sky://extensions/installed` and `sky://extensions/uninstalled` handlers with a try/catch wrapper so a failing command never disrupts the DOM CustomEvent dispatch reserved for Wind orchestration listeners. The Extensions sidebar now reflects newly installed or removed extensions live without requiring a workbench reload.",
			"SHA": "2c5e32336374ec29160c40d6fe8da6badfd735dd"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-26T15:11:53Z",
			"File": [
				"⡟⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				26,
				4
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Land): Advance submodules — Output build-time drag selectors, Wind codegen, Cocoon rebuild, Mountain dep bump\n\nAdvance four Element submodules with a build-time refactor in Output, daily codegen regeneration in Wind, a compiled-output rebuild in Cocoon, and a CI dependency bump in Mountain.\n\nOutput reworks InjectTauriDragRegion from a runtime stylesheet walker to a build-time CSS source scanner. Since WebKit drops the Chromium-only `-webkit-app-region` declaration at parse time, runtime CSSStyleRule inspection returns empty strings under WKWebView. The new approach extracts drag/no-drag selectors via regex from VS Code's CSS source files on disk at build time and bakes them into the workbench bundle as `globalThis.__LAND_DRAG_SELECTORS__` / `__LAND_NO_DRAG_SELECTORS__` arrays. The runtime polyfill switches from walking stylesheets to iterating these pre-collected lists with querySelectorAll, with an early bail when both arrays are empty. Companion changes: remove the left: 80px drag-region CSS inset from MacTitlebarOffsetCSS (the HTML attribute polyfill handles Tauri hit-testing), add padding-right: 0 assertion to prevent right-edge titlebar drift, improve the triple-signal fullscreen detector, and gate InjectPartZIndexCSS behind DisableUIFixes.\n\nWind regenerates all generated artifacts after upstream VS Code source corrections — CommandCatalog drops from 551 to 550 entries, ServiceCatalog grows from 500 to 502 (adding IChatViewFactory and ISessionsPartService), ISessionsManagementService gains a setActive method, and four per-service upstream files have corrected source line references.\n\nCocoon rebuilds Target/ artifacts after RouteManifest regeneration. Mountain bumps ad-m/github-push-action from 1.1.0 to 1.3.0 via Dependabot.",
			"SHA": "0f281e4508bba88675bb19ea30c7f5ff353fa3ca"
		}
	],
